<item>
            <title>[LU-20285] replaces an indirect heuristic (vui_ra_valid flag) with a direct check of the I/O type (CIT_FAULT)</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20285</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The patch replaces an indirect heuristic (vui_ra_valid flag)&lt;br/&gt;
with a direct check of the I/O type (CIT_FAULT),&lt;br/&gt;
which represents a page fault handling operation&lt;br/&gt;
(typically triggered by mmap&apos;d page access).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;CIT_FAULT explicitly indicates the I/O is happening&lt;br/&gt;
due to a page fault from a memory-mapped region,&lt;br/&gt;
rather than inferring from readahead validity.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="97605">LU-20285</key>
